\title{Sixth Sunday after Pentecost 2026}
\tag{cmc}
\date{2026-07-05}
\author{liamoc}
\quote{
Dóminus fortitúdo plebis suæ, et protéctor salutárium Christi sui est: salvum fac pópulum tuum, Domine, et bénedic hereditáti tuæ, et rege eos usque in sæculum.
}
\p{Today I didn't attend my usual [All Saints Ainslie](https://allsaintsainslie.org.au) as I was visiting Sydney, so I attended [Christ Church St. Laurence](https://ccsl.org.au/) instead. The choir was mens voices who sang the gregorian mass setting \em{cum jubilo} as well as [The Call](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GSvXGIrPYQ8) by Ralph Vaughan Williams, a setting of a poem by Herbert:}
\quote{
  \poem{
    \line{Come, my Way, my Truth, my Life:}
    \line{Such a Way, as gives us breath:}
    \line{Such a Truth, as ends all strife:}
    \line{Such a Life, as killeth death.}
    \line{\br}
    \line{Come, My Light, my Feast, my Strength:}
    \line{Such a Light, as shows a feast:}
    \line{Such a Feast, as mends in length:}
    \line{Such a Strength, as makes his guest.}
    \line{\br}
    \line{Come, my Joy, my Love, my Heart:}
    \line{Such a Joy, as none can move:}
    \line{Such a Love, as none can part:}
    \line{Such a Heart, as joys in love.  }}
}
\p{It was a very restorative service, even for my (Buddhist) in-laws. I believe that my usual choir performed "Thee we adore" by T. Frederick H. Candlyn in my absence, an arrangement of \em{adoro te devote}.}
